{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-719", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/719", "wordCount": 3417, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Welcome to What's New in File"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Management and Quick Look."}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "We have a lot of great new API"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "for managing documents and file"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "previews to share with you"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "today."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "Here are the areas that we're going to cover in this session."}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "First, we'll show how your app"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "can use the document picker to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "access a directory and its"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "We'll also show how your app can"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "properly support files stored on"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "external USB drives or SMB"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "servers."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "Then also, see how your app can"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "fetch and display rich"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "thumbnails."}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "And you'll see how your app can"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "provide quick editing support"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "for images, PDFs, and videos via"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "Quick Look."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "We've made it easy to port your"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "iOS app to macOS as the Quick"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "Look Extension APIs are now"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "cross platform."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "And finally, we'll talk about"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "supporting iPad apps on Mac."}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "So who is this session for?"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "If you are writing a new app or"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "already have an app that"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "presents documents or performs"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "file operations, you're in the"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "right session. You want to learn the best"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "practices to support files"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "stored on removable drives, such"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "as USB and SMB."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "You may also need your app to"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "recursively access multiple"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "documents within a folder and"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "perform batch file operations."}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "Stick around if you want to"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "learn more about displaying file"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "thumbnails or if you want to"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "provide simple image and video"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "editing in your app."}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "By the way, if you haven't"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "checked it out yet, you should"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "definitely take a look at"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "Managing Documents in Your iOS"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "Apps session from WWDC 2018 in"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "which we detailed step-by-step"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "how to use the UIDocumentBrowserViewController"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "and the UIDocumentPickerViewController."}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "There's also a session, Quick"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "Look Previews from the Ground Up"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "from WWDC 2018, which we highly"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "encourage you to watch if you're"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "interested in presenting file"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "previews on iOS and now macOS."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "One of the most requested"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "features has been to access an"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "entire directory and its"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "contents."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "We're really excited that an iOS"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "13 you now can."}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "Features of your app may need to"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "access content of a directory"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "for reading, writing, or"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "creating documents."}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "For instance, an image editor"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "that needs to apply the same"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "change on a batch of images"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "would read every image, apply"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "modifications, and save a new"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "image right next to the"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "original. Prior to iOS 13, an app could"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "access files outside of its"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "application container via the"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "but the user had to pick one"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "file at a time."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "New in iOS 13, your app can"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "present a UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "to let the user pick a folder."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "After validation, your app will"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "be granted recursive access to"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "the directory as well as all of"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "its contents."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "Additionally, you can now set"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "the default directory that is"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "shown on the document picker"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "when presented."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "Now let's take a look at how you"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "can do that now using a few"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "examples of how to configure the"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "UIDocumentPickerViewController."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "To allow folder selection,"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "creating instance initialized"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "with an array containing only"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "the kUTTypeFolder type and then"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "present it."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "To set the default directory of"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "instance, set its directoryURL"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "property and then present."}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "Now let's take a look at this"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "example."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "We show you how to enumerate the"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "contents of a folder, but you"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "can use the same example to"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "write a file here using standard"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "File Manager API."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "Also, make sure to use URL start"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "and stopAccessing"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "SecurityScopedResource calls and"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "use NSFileCoordinator API for"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "reading and writing operations"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "as you can see in the example."}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "In iOS 13, users are in control"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "of which applications have"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "access to folders."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "This access is listed and can be"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "revoked in the privacy pane"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "under the Files and Folder"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "section."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "Be aware that because users can"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "revoke access at any time, you"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "need to make sure that your code"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "gracefully handles errors when"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "attempting to open documents or"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "when enumerating folders."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "In this example, you can see how"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "you can maintain persistent"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "access to a folder across"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "application launches by storing"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "bookmark data and then"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "recreating the URL using the URL"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "resolvingBookmarkData options"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "call."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "New in iOS 13, we've added"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "support for external USB drives,"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "thumb drives, and SMB servers."}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "Drives formatted as APFS, HFS+,"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "FAT and ExFAT are supported."}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "Drives can be plugged in either"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "on the USBC connector on the"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "iPad Pro or via the SD card"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "reader attachment."}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "They are automatically listed in"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "the sidebar of the files app or"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "in your app with the"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "or document browser."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "Users can also connect to SMB"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "servers using the Connect to"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "Server action using the same"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "keyboard shortcut as finder or"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "using the sidebar menu."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "Any client of"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "UIDocumentBrowserViewController"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "API or"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "API get the same support for"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "free as long as the app was"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "built using the iOS 13 SDK or"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "later."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "However, there are few things"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "you need to check to make sure"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "your app has great support for"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "USB and SMB."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "There are few assumptions that"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "are no longer true."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "File access is no longer on a"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "single volume because they can"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "now be stored on external"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "volumes, such as USB drives or"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "SMB servers."}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "Volumes can disappear if the USB"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "drive is unplugged or if the"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "network connection to an SMB"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "server volume is lost."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "Disk access can be slower than"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "what you expected in the past."}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "An operation that you would"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "assume is instant can now take"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "several seconds or even minutes"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "depending on the network"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "conditions or the speed of the"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "USB device."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "Also, don't assume the"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "underlying file system is always"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "APFS or HFS+."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "So how does this affect your"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "app?"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "If you need to move a file from"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "one location to another, use the"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "FileManager.moveItem at API and"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "this will take care of moving"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "files across volumes for you."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "In the past, move and clone"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "operations were always fast."}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "When moving across volumes, the"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "operation can become slower copy"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "and delete."}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "If you use NSTemporaryDirectory"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "to save a temporary version of a"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "file, you should update your"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "code to choose the location of"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "the temporary folder based on"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "the ultimate destination of the"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "files written in it."}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "You can do this with the"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "following File Manager call,"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "File Manager URL for"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "itemReplacementDirectory in"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "userDomainMask appropriateFor"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "URL."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "This will always give you the"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "right temporary directory to"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "write files, to."}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "In the past, your app may have"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "assumed that a file may never"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "disappear while it is open and"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "this is no longer true because"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "USB drives can be unplugged and"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "SMB server connections can be"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "interrupted."}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "This may cause your app to fail"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "while reading or writing file"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "contents."}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "Your app should check for errors"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "and fail gracefully."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "One suggestion is if your app"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "fails to write a file, it could"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "present a UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "to let the user choose an"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "alternate location to save the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "file. Reading or writing a file stored"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "on a USB drive or on a distant"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "SMB server can be slow so you"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "need to make sure your app"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "doesn't hang while performing a"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "file operation."}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "Always perform file system"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "operations on a background"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "queue."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "We also recommend that you add"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "UI like an activity indicator to"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "let the user know something is"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "happening, and offering a way"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "for your user to cancel the"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "operation is a great idea."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "Otherwise the user might feel"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "like the application is"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "unresponsive."}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "When a document is stored on a"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "USB drive or remote SMB server,"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "LIFS is reported instead of the"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "file system the media is"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "formatted as."}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "It's likely that your app should"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "not worry about the underlying"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "file system."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "Instead you should check the"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "file system capabilities to know"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "which file system operations are"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "supported."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "LIFS is a file system"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "abstraction and it do not look"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "for its presence directly."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "To know more about LIFS, we"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "recommend that you look at the"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "What's New in File Systems"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "New in iOS 13, there's"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "additional customization support"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "in UIDocumentBrowserViewController."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "Let's take a look at this now."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "Now, you can choose to always"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "show file extensions by setting"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "the shouldShowFileExtensions"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "property to true."}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "The Create Document button can"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "now also be customized to adjust"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "the aspect ratio of the button"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "icon by setting the"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "defaultDocumentAspectRatio"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "And the button titled Text can"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "now be changed by setting the"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "localizedCreate"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "DocumentActionTitle property."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "And now Lyn will talk about"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "What's New in Quick Look."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "Fetching File Thumbnails in"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "Your App."}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "This is for those of you who"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "want to enhance the appearance"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "of your application by"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "displaying rich file thumbnails."}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "So instead of something like"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "this, you could have something"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "like this."}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "Quick Look thumbnailing is a new"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "cross platform framework for"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "retrieving thumbnail images for"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "file URLs."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "This is new functionality on iOS"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "and replaces the C API for"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "QLThumbnail on macOS."}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "It also replaces"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "NSURLThumbnailDictionaryKey."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "iOS and macOS provide built-in"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "support for several file types,"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "such as images, PDFs, text"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "files, videos, et cetera."}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "You can also provide support for"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "your own file types with"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "thumbnail extensions."}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "Quick Look thumbnailing is"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "non-UI framework."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "We don't import UIKit or AppKit"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "by default."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "We can get CGImages of your"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "thumbnail without either but you"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "can also obtain UIImages on iOS"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "or NSImages on macOS by"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "explicitly linking UIKit or"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "AppKit respectively."}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "It is asynchronous so it won't"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "block while retrieving the"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "thumbnail and it supports"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "cancellation in case you decide"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "you don't want that thumbnail"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "after all."}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "Let's start with a big picture"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "overview."}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "To get a thumbnail, you start by"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "creating a"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "QLThumbnailGenerator.Request and"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "then pass it to a"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "QLThumbnailGenerator specifying"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "if you would like to be notified"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "every time a new representation"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "of the thumbnail is available or"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "only when the best"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "representation you requested is"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "complete."}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "You can request different"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "representations of thumbnails"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "which will have different"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "quality and performance costs."}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "Icon is the generic image"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "associated with that file type."}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "This will be the same for all"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "files of a given type."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "Low quality thumbnail is a"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "faster thumbnail that we were"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "able to provide that may not be"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "exactly the size you specified."}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "This typically comes from a"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "cached version of the thumbnail"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "or possibly thumbnails embedded"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "in the file itself."}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "The last representation type"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "thumbnail is a full quality"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "version of the thumbnail,"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "matching the request exactly."}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "This will take the longest to"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "generate."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "For convenience, you can also"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "specify all to get any type of"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "available thumbnail."}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "When you create a QLThumbnail"}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "generation request, you specify"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "size, scale and representation"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "types you would like."}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "You may only care about the full"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "quality thumbnail or you may be"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "OK with an icon or lower quality"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "version. It's best to specify all"}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "representation types that will"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "work for you as not all three"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "types may be available for a"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "given thumbnail."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "You will get a"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "QLThumbnailRepresentation back"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "which will specify the type of"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "thumbnail it is, icon, low"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "quality or thumbnail and an"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "image which can either be"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "accessed as a CGImage, or if"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "you've linked UIKit on iOS or"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "AppKit on macOS, you can get a"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "UIImage or NS Image"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "respectively."}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "To get that"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "QLThumbnailRepresentation, you"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "pass your thumbnail request to a"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "QLThumbnailGenerator."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "If you just want the best"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "quality thumbnail available, use"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "generateBestRepresentation."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "This will call your completion"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "handler with the best version of"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "your thumbnail request that"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "could be created."}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "Or you may prefer to get"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "incremental updates by providing"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "an updateHandler to generate"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "representations that will be"}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "called as each representation"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "becomes available."}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "You can use this, for example,"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "to update your UI quickly and"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "then improve the quality of what"}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "is shown as better thumbnails"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "arrive."}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "So that's enough about thumbnail"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "retrieval."}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "Let's talk about using Quick"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "Look to edit images, PDFs and"}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "videos."}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "Quick Look provides API to"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "preview documents of various"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "types of files on iOS."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "It also allows you to provide"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "custom previews for your own"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "documents via extensions."}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "Now in iOS 13, we've also added"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "support to quickly edit images,"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "PDFs and videos with the"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "QLPreviewController."}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "The QLPreviewController is what"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "you use to preview a file."}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "To make use if it simply"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "allocate an instance of"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "QLPreviewController and set a"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "data source and delegate before"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "presenting it."}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "To learn more about Quick Look"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "and the QLPreviewController, we"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "highly encourage you to check"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "out our WWDC presentation from"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "2018 Quick Look Previews from"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "the Ground Up."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "New to iOS 13, the"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "QLPreviewController also"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "provides access to Markup, the"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "editing tools available when you"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "preview a document and files or"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "edit an attachment in mail."}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "This is available for images and"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "PDFs. QLPreviewController also"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "provides support for trimming"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "and rotating videos."}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "To use these features, you just"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "have to enable editing mode."}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "All you have to do is implement"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "an optional delegate method"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "editing mode for preview item."}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "By default, editing is disabled"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "but it is possible to enable it"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "on a per item basis."}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "This delegate method allows you"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "to specify both if you want"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "editing capabilities and how you"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "want to handle the resulting"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "You can have the"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "QLPreviewController overwrite"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "the original file with the"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "user's edited version."}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "To do so, return updateContents"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "from editing mode for preview"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "item."}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "If you need to react to edits"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "being successfully saved, you"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "can also implement the optional"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "didUpdateContentsof previewItem"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "method."}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "Or you may prefer to use"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "QLPreviewController to create"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "edited copies of the files being"}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "previewed and manage them"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "yourself."}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "To do so return createCopy from"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "editing mode for preview item"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "and implement the delegate"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "method that saved edited copy of"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "preview item at modified"}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "contents URL."}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "Quick Look Extension APIs on"}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "So we've just talked about"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "getting and using thumbnails and"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "previews for files."}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "Now let's talk about how to"}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "provide thumbnails and previews"}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "for your own file types."}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "Already on iOS, an app can"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "implement a Quick Look thumbnail"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "and preview extension to provide"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "systemwide thumbnail and preview"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "support for its own documents."}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "Now the same Quick Look"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "extension API is available on"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "Thumbnails are used throughout"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "macOS and iOS to allow users to"}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "identify files quickly."}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "For instance, you can see on the"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "screenshot how macOS makes use"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "of them in Finder."}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "MacOS can generate thumbnails"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "for many common file types, but"}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "implementing a thumbnail"}, {"start": 987.0, "text": "extension allows you to also"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "provide thumbnails for your own"}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "file types so that they can have"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "a rich representation in Finder"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "and elsewhere a thumbnail might"}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "show. The extension API replaces the"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "old CF plug-in based generator"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "If you have a Quick Look"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "generator, consider migrating"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "soon."}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "I say Quick Look extension in a"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "general sense here as the"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "thumbnail extension point comes"}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "from Quick Look thumbnailing."}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "This was previously vended from"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "the Quick Look framework on iOS"}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "but you might want to consider"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "importing it from the Quick Look"}, {"start": 1018.0, "text": "thumbnailing instead if you do"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "not need UIKit as this will make"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "your extension leaner."}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "To create a thumbnail extension,"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "add a new target in your Xcode"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "project using the thumbnail"}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "extension template."}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "After setting up your extension"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "target, you will be able to"}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "start implementing your"}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "QLThumbnailProvider subclass."}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "You can draw your thumbnail"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "using either a CG context, an"}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "AppKit context, or you can"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "provide a file URL to an image."}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "Here's a quick example where we"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "overwrite the provide thumbnail"}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "for request handler method."}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "We extensively cover this part"}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "of the Quick Look API in our"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "session from WWDC 2017 \"Building"}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "Great Document-based Apps in iOS"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "11\"."}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "We highly encourage you to check"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "it out. In a nutshell, you will get a"}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "QLFileThumbnailRequest which"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "will have the URL of the file,"}, {"start": 1074.0, "text": "the maximum and minimum sizes of"}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "the thumbnail, and its scale."}, {"start": 1078.0, "text": "Use these to create a thumbnail"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "matching those specifications."}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "For each thumbnail request, the"}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "API expects you to create a"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "QLThumbnailReply which will be"}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "used to generate the thumbnail."}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "Pass the QLThumbnailReply to the"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "completion handler above."}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "To debug your thumbnail"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "extension on macOS, you can use"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "QLManage."}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "If you have written Quick Look"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "generators in the past, you may"}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "recognize this tool."}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "Build and run your extension"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "target in Xcode to register your"}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "extension with the system."}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "Then use QLManage to generate a"}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "thumbnail of your file type and"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "attach to your extension in"}, {"start": 1117.0, "text": "Xcode."}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "Preview Extensions for Files."}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "New this year, Quick Look on"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "macOS also allows you to provide"}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "previews for your own file types"}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "by implementing a preview"}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "extension."}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "Quick Look preview extensions"}, {"start": 1133.0, "text": "already existed to support Core"}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "Spotlight previews."}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "See WWDC 2017's What's New in"}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "Core Spotlight for iOS and"}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 1142.0, "text": "This year we've also added"}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "support for file previews."}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "With the extension, you can now"}, {"start": 1147.0, "text": "directly provide a view to"}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "display your preview."}, {"start": 1151.0, "text": "This is different from the old"}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "Quick Look generators in which"}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "you provided data or a URL for"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "the system to present."}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "The new extension API allows you"}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "greater control over the"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "appearance of your preview."}, {"start": 1162.0, "text": "We recommend you migrate off the"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "old Quick Look generators as"}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "they will be deprecated in a"}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "future release."}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "To create a Preview Extension,"}, {"start": 1172.0, "text": "add a new target in your project"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "and select the Preview Extension"}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "template."}, {"start": 1178.0, "text": "The API is identical to iOS"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "Preview extensions. See WWDC 2018's Quick Look"}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "Previews from the Ground Up."}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "As a quick summary, you will"}, {"start": 1188.0, "text": "want to declare the list of"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "supported UTIs in"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "QLSupportedContentTypes in your"}, {"start": 1193.0, "text": "Info.plist."}, {"start": 1194.0, "text": "This must exactly match the UTIs"}, {"start": 1197.0, "text": "of the files you want previewed."}, {"start": 1199.0, "text": "Matching by parent UTI is not"}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "supported."}, {"start": 1202.0, "text": "The template will provide a view"}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "controller which will be what"}, {"start": 1205.0, "text": "you prepare your preview in."}, {"start": 1207.0, "text": "Here's a quick example of the"}, {"start": 1210.0, "text": "view controller template."}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "Implement, preparePreviewofFile"}, {"start": 1214.0, "text": "at URL to prepare your view"}, {"start": 1216.0, "text": "controller. And once you're ready, call the"}, {"start": 1218.0, "text": "completion handler."}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "The QLPreviewView presenting you"}, {"start": 1221.0, "text": "preview will show a spinning"}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "wheel until this completion"}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "handler is called."}, {"start": 1225.0, "text": "So get your preview ready as"}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "quickly as possible."}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "Keep in mind, your preview can"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "be shown in any QLPreviewView"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "which may be the Preview panel,"}, {"start": 1236.0, "text": "the Column View sidebar,"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "Spotlight or any client of the"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "QLPreviewView at all."}, {"start": 1245.0, "text": "To debug, launch your extension"}, {"start": 1247.0, "text": "target with Xcode."}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "Note that Xcode will lunch the"}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "Quick Look simulator by default."}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "This is to aid in debugging Core"}, {"start": 1254.0, "text": "Spotlight previews which are"}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "extension can also provide"}, {"start": 1257.0, "text": "support for."}, {"start": 1258.0, "text": "To debug regular file previews,"}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "you can ignore the simulator and"}, {"start": 1262.0, "text": "invoke your preview with finder"}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "or QLManage."}, {"start": 1264.0, "text": "As long as your preview"}, {"start": 1265.0, "text": "extension is launched through"}, {"start": 1267.0, "text": "Xcode, Xcode will automatically"}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "attach to it."}, {"start": 1274.0, "text": "Let's talk about supporting iPad"}, {"start": 1276.0, "text": "apps on Mac."}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "Our document handling APIs are"}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "supported in iPad apps on Mac so"}, {"start": 1282.0, "text": "you can bring your document-based iOS apps to"}, {"start": 1284.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "For UIDocumentPickerViewController"}, {"start": 1290.0, "text": "use it as you would on iOS and"}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "users will automatically get and"}, {"start": 1293.0, "text": "experience that feels native to"}, {"start": 1296.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 1297.0, "text": "Specifically, the .import and"}, {"start": 1298.0, "text": ".open modes show an NSOpenPanel"}, {"start": 1301.0, "text": "and the .exportToService and"}, {"start": 1303.0, "text": ".moveToService modes show an"}, {"start": 1305.0, "text": "NSSavePanel."}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "Similarly, for"}, {"start": 1309.0, "text": "UIDocumentBrowserViewController,"}, {"start": 1312.0, "text": "users will get an experience"}, {"start": 1313.0, "text": "that feels native for a"}, {"start": 1314.0, "text": "document-based app on macOS."}, {"start": 1316.0, "text": "The user will get an NSOpenPanel"}, {"start": 1319.0, "text": "in a separate window just like"}, {"start": 1320.0, "text": "they do in TextEdit."}, {"start": 1322.0, "text": "There are a few minor runtime"}, {"start": 1324.0, "text": "differences due to differences"}, {"start": 1326.0, "text": "between the interfaces on iOS"}, {"start": 1328.0, "text": "and macOS."}, {"start": 1329.0, "text": "A good example of this is the"}, {"start": 1331.0, "text": "UIDocumentBrowserViewControllers"}, {"start": 1332.0, "text": "navigation bar which doesn't"}, {"start": 1334.0, "text": "exist on macOS."}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "Check the documentation for"}, {"start": 1337.0, "text": "details on what to do for these"}, {"start": 1339.0, "text": "particular cases."}, {"start": 1341.0, "text": "In some cases, you can use new"}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "APIs, such as the menu bar API,"}, {"start": 1345.0, "text": "to help you address these UI"}, {"start": 1346.0, "text": "differences."}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "Quick Look is also available on"}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "iPad apps on Mac."}, {"start": 1354.0, "text": "Presenting a QLPreviewController"}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "will launch a QLPreviewPanel on"}, {"start": 1358.0, "text": "macOS to provide a more native"}, {"start": 1360.0, "text": "Mac experience."}, {"start": 1362.0, "text": "Since the QLPreviewPanel is a"}, {"start": 1364.0, "text": "separate window, you're"}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "presenting view controllers"}, {"start": 1366.0, "text": "content will be visible but it"}, {"start": 1368.0, "text": "will be great out and"}, {"start": 1369.0, "text": "non-interactive."}, {"start": 1372.0, "text": "Test your iPad apps on Mac to"}, {"start": 1374.0, "text": "make sure it looks great."}, {"start": 1378.0, "text": "One limitation to note of"}, {"start": 1379.0, "text": "QLPreviewController in iPad apps"}, {"start": 1381.0, "text": "on Mac is that embedding the"}, {"start": 1383.0, "text": "QLPreviewController's view is"}, {"start": 1385.0, "text": "not fully supported and we will"}, {"start": 1387.0, "text": "provide a thumbnail instead of a"}, {"start": 1388.0, "text": "live preview in this case."}, {"start": 1393.0, "text": "So what have we learned today?"}, {"start": 1394.0, "text": "First, we've shown you how to"}, {"start": 1396.0, "text": "leverage new features of iOS 13"}, {"start": 1398.0, "text": "in your app, such as accessing"}, {"start": 1400.0, "text": "multiple files in a directory,"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "supporting USB drives and SMB"}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "servers."}, {"start": 1405.0, "text": "Then we've taken a look at using"}, {"start": 1407.0, "text": "Quick Look to display the same"}, {"start": 1409.0, "text": "rich thumbnails as in the files"}, {"start": 1411.0, "text": "app, provide Quick Look editing"}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "support for images and videos,"}, {"start": 1414.0, "text": "and provide previews and"}, {"start": 1416.0, "text": "thumbnails with modern extension"}, {"start": 1417.0, "text": "API on the Mac."}]}
